originally copied from that exact revision.

Ported implementation families and their upstream origins:
- src/chains.ts, src/client.ts, src/pools.ts, src/positions.ts,
  src/prices.ts, src/quotes.ts, src/tokens.ts, src/transactions.ts:
  sugar/chains.py and its pool, position, price, quote and token modules.
- src/config.ts and src/known-tokens.ts: sugar/config.py.
- src/helpers.ts: sugar/helpers.py and sugar/quote.py.
- src/models.ts and src/types.ts: sugar/pool.py, sugar/position.py,
  sugar/token.py, sugar/price.py, sugar/deposit.py, sugar/withdraw.py,
  sugar/quote.py and sugar/config.py.
- src/planner.ts: sugar/swap.py.
- src/superswap.ts: sugar/superswap.py.
- src/actions.ts and the original CLI behavior: sugar/cli.py.
- src/abis.ts and original ABI artifacts: sugar/abi.py and sugar/abis/.

At review time, these JSON artifacts were byte-identical to the inspected
Python SDK reference: bridge_get_fee, bridge_transfer_remote, gauge_basic,
gauge_cl, interchain_account_router, interchain_router, nfpm, pool_basic,
price_oracle, quoter, router, slipstream, sugar, sugar_rewards and swapper.
Their paths are src/abis/<name>.json and upstream sugar/abis/<name>.json.
The current erc20.json differs from the upstream reference. Additional
permit2, pool_cl, rewards_distributor, ve_sugar, voter, voting_escrow and
voting_reward artifacts require a separate exact-source provenance check.
ABI attribution does not grant rights to underlying contract implementations.

